<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIAN RETAIL SALES FALL 15 PCT IN JANUARY.</title>
<headline>ROMANIAN RETAIL SALES FALL 15 PCT IN JANUARY.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover from Romanian retail trading fell by 15 percent in January from the same month of 1996, National Statistics Board data showed on Monday.</p>
<p>It said sales of food produce, beverages and tobacco dropped by 15.9 percent from January 1996.</p>
<p>The private sector accounted for 71 percent of January's reatil trade, down from 72.8 percent in January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
